---
import ServiceLayout from '../layouts/ServiceLayout.astro';
import { faqs } from '../config/faqs';

const description =
	'Professionally integrated Lutron lighting for Colorado homes: dimmers, keypads, scenes, and schedules that belong to the architecture.';
---

<ServiceLayout
	title="Lutron Lighting Installation"
	description={description}
	eyebrow="Lighting"
	heading="Lutron lighting, designed into the house."
	lede="Keypads, dimmers, and scenes replace a collection of smart bulbs. The room recalls a setting. Guests do not need an app to turn on a light."
	crumb="Lutron Lighting"
	serviceName="Lutron lighting installation"
	serviceType="Lutron lighting installation"
	faqs={faqs.lutron}
	ctaLabel="Design Your Smart Home"
	ctaTitle="Design the lighting."
	ctaText="Bring the way the rooms are used. The keypads and scenes are drawn from that, not from a default program."
	related={[
		{ href: '/motorized-shades/', label: 'Motorized shades', text: 'Daylight and electric light, specified as one design.' },
		{ href: '/smart-home-automation/', label: 'Smart home', text: 'Josh.ai and the rest of the control layer, when you want them.' },
		{ href: '/unifi-networking/', label: 'The network', text: 'Remote access and integrations assume the network is real.' },
	]}
>
	<section class="section" aria-labelledby="problem-heading">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<h2 id="problem-heading">This is not a DIY bulb project.</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					Consumer bulbs are easy to buy and tiring to live with. They fall offline, they disagree about what
					“evening” means, and they ask every person in the house to carry the same app. Lutron lighting is the
					other tradition: equipment designed into the rooms, commissioned as a system, and left alone.
				</p>
				<p>
					Solutions are built with Lutron technology. That is not a claim of authorized-dealer or certified-installer
					status.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-cream" aria-labelledby="scope-heading">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2 id="scope-heading">What a lighting design can cover.</h2>
			<ul class="index-list">
				<li>
					<strong>Control</strong>
					<p>Smart dimmers, keypads, and whole-home lighting control, including occupancy and vacancy behavior where it helps.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Scenes</strong>
					<p>Morning, evening, entertainment, and away — the settings you will actually recall, not a catalog of twenty.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Schedules</strong>
					<p>Exterior lighting and interior paths that follow the day without a nightly routine of tapping a phone.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Shades and network</strong>
					<p>
						When shades are in the project, scenes can coordinate both. The network is planned so remote features are
						not the fragile part of the house.
					</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" aria-labelledby="keypad-heading">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<h2 id="keypad-heading">A keypad is the interface that does not expire.</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					Engraved buttons for the scenes that matter let anyone operate the room. The app is there for changes and
					for remote use. It is not required to walk in and have light. That distinction is the difference between
					a gadget and a finish.
				</p>
				<p>
					If voice control across lighting, shades, and other systems is part of the brief, Josh.ai can sit above
					this layer. It is optional. Integration depends on the equipment selected for the house.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-cream" aria-labelledby="together-heading">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<h2 id="together-heading">Light and shade, as one gesture.</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					Morning: selected shades rise and the lighting eases back. Evening: shades lower and interior light takes
					over. A film: shades close and the room dims. Those are design choices, made when both systems are in the
					project. A lighting-only house is not described as if the windows already move.
				</p>
				<p>
					See <a href="/motorized-shades/">motorized shades</a> for the daylight side of the same idea.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</ServiceLayout>
